## Layout

```
{{ name }}/
├── forge.yml          # project configuration
├── src/               # source under test
│   ├── example.c
│   └── example.h
├── test/              # test_*.c files (Unity)
│   └── test_example.c
└── mocks/             # auto-generated mocks (do not edit)
```

## Quick start

```bash
vpl test            # discover → compile → run → report (native)
vpl test --coverage # with gcov coverage (native only)
vpl build           # compile only, no run
vpl targets         # list available toolchain profiles
vpl mock src/foo.h  # generate mocks/mock_foo.{c,h}
```

The convention is `test/test_<module>.c` tests `src/<module>.c`. Add a new module
by creating `src/<module>.{c,h}` and `test/test_<module>.c`, then run `vpl test`.
